{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hecke-mass-element","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:hecke-mass-element","kind":"definition","title":"Hecke mass element","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-identity","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-hecke-algebra-from-braiding","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-jones-markov-trace"],"tags":["hecke-algebra","mass","frobenius-hopf","fibre-functor","schur-weyl"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Torsion.HeckeMassElement","text":"hecke-mass-element.md","leanSource":"hecke-mass-element.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:hecke-mass-element\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a\n<a href=\"#def:quantum-observable-universe\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/qou-definition\">quantum observable universe</a> with\nHecke algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(R, q)</code>\n(<a href=\"#rem:hecke-algebra-from-braiding\" data-at=\"braids-and-knots/categorical-braiding-hecke-eigenbasis/categorical-braiding-markov-trace-nf\">Hecke algebra</a>) and Markov trace\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_M \\colon H_n(R, q) \\to k</code>\n(<a href=\"#thm:jones-markov-trace\" data-at=\"braids-and-knots/categorical-braiding-hecke-eigenbasis/categorical-braiding-hecke-quotient\">Jones--Markov trace</a>).</p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varrho \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A</code> be a vortex morphism with braid\nrepresentative <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\in B_n</code>.  The <strong>mass integrand</strong>\n(<a href=\"#def:mass-identity\" data-at=\"mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-opener/mass-endomorphism-mass-identity\">mass identity</a>) is the composition</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\alpha_\\varrho\n  =\n  (\\textstyle\\int_A \\otimes \\mathrm{id})\n  \\circ \\Delta\n  \\circ \\varrho\n  \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A,</code></pre>\n<p>and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_{\\alpha_\\varrho} \\in \\mathrm{End}_{\\mathbf{C}}(A)</code> is left multiplication by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha_\\varrho</code> in the Frobenius--Hopf algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>.</p>\n<p>The <strong>Hecke mass element</strong> of the vortex <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varrho</code> is</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Phi_{\\mathrm{mass}}(\\beta)\n  \\;:=\\;\n  \\tau\\bigl(L_{\\alpha_\\varrho}\\bigr)\n  \\;\\in\\; H_n(R, q).</code></pre>\n<p>Its <strong>descended</strong> and <strong>transient</strong> parts are</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Phi^{\\mathrm{desc}}(\\beta) := \\tau\\bigl(\\hat{\\tau}_n(L_{\\alpha_\\varrho})\\bigr),\n  \\qquad\n  \\Phi^{\\mathrm{trans}}(\\beta) := \\tau\\bigl(L_{\\alpha_\\varrho} - \\hat{\\tau}_n(L_{\\alpha_\\varrho})\\bigr),</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hat{\\tau}_n</code> is the <a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-descent\">descent</a> involution (<a href=\"#prop:descent-eigenspaces\"><a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-descent\">descent</a> eigenspaces</a>).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-element.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.1.7","page":"b/def-hecke-mass-element","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":65},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:HeckeTemperleyLieb.HeckeMassElement.HeckeMassElement","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hecke-mass-element.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
